{"overview":"Filmic insert to Eisenstein's modernized, free adaptation of Ostrovskiy's 19th-century Russian stage play, \"The Wise Man\" (\"Na vsyakogo mudretsa dovolno prostoty\"). The anti-hero Glumov tries to escape exposure in the midst of acrobatics, derring-do, and farcical clowning. Several members of Eisenstein's troupe at the legendary \"Proletkult\" stage theatre in Moscow briefly appear in this little film.","cast":[{"n":"Grigori Aleksandrov","c":"Glumov 2","p":"/A8LitAachroJZ2wQq4mdbB698WS.jpg","q":"Q561459"},{"n":"Aleksandr Antonov","c":"Joffre","p":"/2SsBRWuIQr3T0Ou7K75HarJoNIo.jpg","q":null},{"n":"Sergei Eisenstein","c":"Sergei Eisenstein","p":"/ks9uuDtKu9m9w50t18PamLZ91to.jpg","q":"Q8003"},{"n":"Ivan Yazykanov","c":"Glumov 1","p":null,"q":null},{"n":"Maksim Shtraukh","c":"Milyukov-Mamaev","p":"/dNJR5w6SAGLEQCXjcI19bR752NN.jpg","q":null},{"n":"Vera Yanukova","c":"Mamaeva","p":"/gd3LQ1mkVDLpRxHb1Qe0Qb2GpbL.jpg","q":"Q130286183"},{"n":"Mikhail Gomorov","c":"Turusina","p":"/lXCarRbaWNwYFTZXTY5llc1nKPP.jpg","q":"Q4143015"},{"n":"Very Muzykant","c":"Mashenka","p":null,"q":null},{"n":"Ivan Pyryev","c":"Fascist Clown","p":"/dI1vaz8LXaDReLOYg500d0hd4GY.jpg","q":"Q552450"},{"n":"Aleksandr Pavlovich Antonov","c":"","p":null,"q":"Q203639"}],"country":["Soviet Union"],"wiki":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glumov%27s_Diary","qid":"Q3223723","rel":{"RU":{"d":"1923-05-21"}}}